WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.334 --> 00:00:23.967
While the secret garden was coming alive and two children were coming alive with it, Mr. Craven was wandering through Europe.

2
00:00:23.968 --> 00:00:28.230
He had traveled through the beautiful mountains of Switzerland.

3
00:00:28.231 --> 00:00:31.856
He had seen the magnificent Norwegian fjords.

4
00:00:31.857 --> 00:00:38.616
But his heart was still broken, and he could not shake the dark thoughts and nightmares from his mind.

5
00:00:38.617 --> 00:00:43.487
One day he was hiking in Austria when he decided to rest by a stream.

6
00:00:43.488 --> 00:00:50.180
Mr. Craven did not know how long he sat there on the carpet of green moss, looking at the birds and the flowers.

7
00:00:50.181 --> 00:00:53.790
The sunlight seemed to wash over him.

8
00:00:53.791 --> 00:00:57.035
"What's happening?" he whispered.

9
00:00:57.036 --> 00:01:00.864
"I feel . . . Why, it's almost as if I were awakening!"

10
00:01:00.865 --> 00:01:10.077
Months later he would find out that this was the very day when Colin stood in the garden and said, "I'm going to live forever and ever!"

11
00:01:10.078 --> 00:01:16.115
As summer changed into autumn, Mr. Craven moved on to Lake Como in Italy.

12
00:01:16.116 --> 00:01:20.649
He was starting to sleep better, and his dreams no longer terrified him.

13
00:01:20.650 --> 00:01:25.242
He began to think of Misselthwaite and wonder if he should go home.

14
00:01:25.243 --> 00:01:29.679
But every time he thought of Colin, he was reminded of his wife.

15
00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:32.431
He couldn't go home yet.

16
00:01:32.432 --> 00:01:35.585
One night he sat outside by the lake.

17
00:01:35.586 --> 00:01:41.091
The moonlight turned everything to silver. Mr. Craven fell asleep.

18
00:01:41.092 --> 00:01:47.998
In his dreams he heard a voice calling him. "Archie! Archie!"

19
00:01:47.999 --> 00:01:54.151
It was a sweet and lovely voice that he instantly recognized as his wife's.

20
00:01:54.152 --> 00:01:56.953
"Where are you?"

21
00:01:56.954 --> 00:01:59.208
"In the garden."

22
00:01:59.209 --> 00:02:03.318
The dream ended there, but he did not wake up until morning.

23
00:02:03.319 --> 00:02:08.777
A servant appeared by his side and handed him a letter from Dickon's mother.

24
00:02:08.778 --> 00:02:16.122
Dear Sir: Please come home. I think you will be glad if you do.

25
00:02:16.123 --> 00:02:23.025
If you will excuse me, sir, I think your lady would ask you to come if she was here.

26
00:02:23.026 --> 00:02:26.998
Sincerely, Susan Sowerby

27
00:02:26.999 --> 00:02:30.071
Mr. Craven remembered his dream.

28
00:02:30.072 --> 00:02:37.392
"I must go home to Misselthwaite at once," he said to the servant.

29
00:02:37.393 --> 00:02:44.639
When Mr. Craven finally arrived at the manor, he immediately sent for Mrs. Medlock.

30
00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:47.183
"How is Colin?"

31
00:02:47.184 --> 00:02:50.474
Mrs. Medlock didn't know how to respond.

32
00:02:50.475 --> 00:02:58.689
"To tell the truth, sir," she said nervously, "he might be better and he might be worse.

33
00:02:58.690 --> 00:03:05.651
No one can understand why he eats or doesn't eat. He likes Mary and Dickon.

34
00:03:05.652 --> 00:03:12.251
Every day he goes outside with them, but no one knows what they do or where they go."

35
00:03:12.252 --> 00:03:14.434
"Where is Colin now?"

36
00:03:14.435 --> 00:03:18.148
"In one of the gardens, I suppose."

37
00:03:18.149 --> 00:03:23.133
"In the garden," Mr. Craven repeated as he stood up.

38
00:03:23.134 --> 00:03:30.499
He felt as if he were being pulled toward the garden that he had locked up ten years ago.

39
00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:34.501
He went outside and walked past the old fountain.

40
00:03:34.502 --> 00:03:38.846
Flowers surrounded it now, and it was filled with water.

41
00:03:38.847 --> 00:03:43.005
He turned down the long path outside the walled gardens.

42
00:03:43.006 --> 00:03:47.215
He knew where the door was, even though it was hidden by ivy.

43
00:03:47.216 --> 00:03:49.777
But could he find the key?

44
00:03:49.778 --> 00:03:52.126
He stopped and listened.

45
00:03:52.127 --> 00:03:59.302
No one had passed through that door in ten years, yet it sounded like children were laughing in the garden.

46
00:03:59.303 --> 00:04:05.471
Was this another dream? At that moment the door to the garden flew open.

47
00:04:05.472 --> 00:04:09.910
A boy ran out and crashed right into Mr. Craven.

48
00:04:09.911 --> 00:04:12.562
Mr. Craven stared at the boy.

49
00:04:12.563 --> 00:04:18.431
His eyes were so dark, so like her eyes . . . But it couldn't be.

50
00:04:18.432 --> 00:04:21.910
"Father, I'm Colin," said the boy.

51
00:04:21.911 --> 00:04:27.028
"I know you can't believe it. I can scarcely believe it myself."

52
00:04:27.029 --> 00:04:32.518
"In the garden," said Mr. Craven, unable to say anything else.

53
00:04:32.519 --> 00:04:35.877
"Yes. It was the garden that made me well.

54
00:04:35.878 --> 00:04:40.318
And Mary. And Dickon and his creatures. And magic."

55
00:04:40.319 --> 00:04:45.148
Colin was breathless from running, and his words came tumbling out.

56
00:04:45.149 --> 00:04:48.951
"I'm really well. I just beat Mary in a race.

57
00:04:48.952 --> 00:04:53.521
Father, I'm going to live forever and ever. Aren't you glad?"

58
00:04:53.522 --> 00:04:57.093
Mr. Craven did not know what to say for a moment.

59
00:04:57.094 --> 00:05:03.190
He put his hands on Colin's shoulders. "You must tell me all about it."

60
00:05:03.191 --> 00:05:06.954
And so Colin led him into the secret garden.

61
00:05:06.955 --> 00:05:15.220
Mr. Craven looked around, just as Colin had done his first time there, marveling at the roses and other flowers.

62
00:05:15.221 --> 00:05:18.371
"I thought it would all be dead."

63
00:05:18.372 --> 00:05:25.056
Mary and Dickon sat with Mr. Craven while Colin told the story of how they brought the garden back to life.

64
00:05:25.057 --> 00:05:29.993
Ben Weatherstaff was there too, but he soon slipped back to the house.

65
00:05:29.994 --> 00:05:34.012
He wanted to be in the servants' hall when Colin returned.

66
00:05:34.013 --> 00:05:37.827
After a while Ben went to the window.

67
00:05:37.828 --> 00:05:41.351
"Look what's coming across the grass."

68
00:05:41.352 --> 00:05:46.647
When Mrs. Medlock looked, she let out a little shriek.

69
00:05:46.648 --> 00:05:50.586
All the other servants ran to the window.

70
00:05:50.587 --> 00:05:55.303
Across the lawn came Mr. Craven, laughing and smiling.

71
00:05:55.304 --> 00:06:09.182
And walking by his side, as tall and straight as any boy, was Colin.
